# 4. Implementation Details

## 4.1 Project Structure
The project is organized as a Django project (`ats_resume`) containing a main app ([resume](file:///Users/jakkaharikeshavareddy/Desktop/Q-spy/django/ats_resume/resume/ats_engine.py#103-128)).

```
ats_resume/
├── manage.py              # CLI entry point
├── db.sqlite3             # Database file
├── ats_resume/            # Project settings
│   ├── settings.py
│   ├── urls.py
│   └── wsgi.py
├── resume/                # Main Application
│   ├── migrations/        # DB schema history
│   ├── templates/         # HTML files
│   ├── admin.py
│   ├── ats_engine.py      # Core NLP Logic
│   ├── forms.py           # Data validation forms
│   ├── latex_generator.py # LaTeX export logic
│   ├── models.py          # Database definitions
│   ├── pdf_generator.py   # PDF export logic
│   ├── urls.py            # App-specific routing
│   └── views.py           # Request handlers
└── requirements.txt       # Dependencies
```

## 4.2 Core Modules

### 4.2.1 [resume/models.py](file:///Users/jakkaharikeshavareddy/Desktop/Q-spy/django/ats_resume/resume/models.py)
This file defines the schema. It uses Django's ORM features like `related_name` to allow easy reverse-lookups (e.g., `resume.work_experiences.all()`).
*Key Insight:* The relationship between `User` and [Resume](file:///Users/jakkaharikeshavareddy/Desktop/Q-spy/django/ats_resume/resume/models.py#7-25) is 1:N, allowing a user to tailor different resumes for different job applications.

### 4.2.2 [resume/views.py](file:///Users/jakkaharikeshavareddy/Desktop/Q-spy/django/ats_resume/resume/views.py)
Contains 20+ view functions handling the application flow.
- [dashboard()](file:///Users/jakkaharikeshavareddy/Desktop/Q-spy/django/ats_resume/resume/views.py#46-67): Aggregates all user resumes and calculates their scores.
- [edit_resume()](file:///Users/jakkaharikeshavareddy/Desktop/Q-spy/django/ats_resume/resume/views.py#206-239): A central hub view that loads all child objects (Education, Projects) for a resume.
- [export_resume_pdf()](file:///Users/jakkaharikeshavareddy/Desktop/Q-spy/django/ats_resume/resume/views.py#415-434): Streams a generated PDF file as an HTTP attachment.

### 4.2.3 [resume/forms.py](file:///Users/jakkaharikeshavareddy/Desktop/Q-spy/django/ats_resume/resume/forms.py)
Utilizes `ModelForm` to generate HTML forms automatically from Models.
*Validation:* Custom validation logic (e.g., limiting Projects to 2 max per resume) ensures data integrity before it reaches the database.

## 4.3 Database Models Highlight
```python
class Resume(models.Model):
    user = models.ForeignKey(User, on_delete=models.CASCADE)
    full_name = models.CharField(max_length=150)
    skills = models.TextField(null=True, blank=True)
    # ... other fields
```

